{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances","id":1544198,"title":"Inheritances","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-18T07:05:21-07:00","id":1544198,"title":"Inheritances","content":"How are people feeling about Inheritances and how they fit the major/minor Path dynamic at the moment?<br /> <br /> in a couple of cases I absolutely can see how they work for reinforcing your vision of the character. Get of Lyka, for example, get to pick between leaning heavily into &quot;grr Werewolf&quot; with bonuses to unarmed attacks and an extra dot in physical, or leaning into the more abstract Hunter thing and getting bonuses to investigate and a dot of mental. <br /> <br /> But for a lot of families, or even whole Lineages, the Inheritance seems to be quite a core part of the fantasy that you don't want to give up.<br /> <br /> Variously:<br /> <br /> All Dead need to choose between their Family inheritance (often tied to the edition they need to feed on) and a resistance to damage that feels like it's intent to what the Dead *are*<br /> <br /> All Hungry need to choose between a regeneration bonus that feels like it should be just part of being a vampire or their Family-specific thing. <br /> <br /> Outcasts can't see the true forms of other Outcasts units they're Lineage-major even though Cassie explicitly says they can all do it in her narration.<br /> <br /> Vondnici can't breathe underwater units they're family-major<br /> <br /> Skimming Sorcerers, the Network at least seem to really *need* their family Inheritance to do their thing although to be fair nothing in the rules says you have to stick to your family's form of sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Basically it often seems like a bit of a false choice and, worse, one that's tied to another false choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T07:19:02-07:00","id":1544199,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I felt that those need to be pointed out to them to change things up via the feedback form.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, I was thinking about this problem.<br /> Give each Family a Major Path and a Minor Path and take out the Lineage Path entirely.<br /> If you choose, say Battleground Angels as your Minor Path, then you get the Inheritance listed for Outcasts. If you choose for it to be a Major Path, you STILL get the Inheritance for Outcasts but you ALSO get the one for Battleground Angels.<br /> You just change the power and adjust some on the Lineage but you still get it. This also solves the point distribution issue involved in the other thread as it allows for far FAR more versatility and lets you play against type as a lot of people prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T10:31:28-07:00","id":1544212,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I don't know. Like the Gaki are supposed to be necromancers, but if the only thing giving them that is their singular ability to summon a phantasm on occasion and that's only some of them it seems hard for me to think of the whole family as necromancers... Is the only reason House Bathory has the reputation as blood bathers because of their inheritance? I'm hopeful that there will be more to reinforce the themes of the families as they get released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T10:54:08-07:00","id":1544214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances?p=1544212#post1544212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I don't know. Like the Gaki are supposed to be necromancers, but if the only thing giving them that is their singular ability to summon a phantasm on occasion and that's only some of them it seems hard for me to think of the whole family as necromancers... Is the only reason House Bathory has the reputation as blood bathers because of their inheritance? I'm hopeful that there will be more to reinforce the themes of the families as they get released.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reserving judgement on the Gaki because there *might* be something like the Abjuration/Binding rules from CofD buried in the Magic or Antagonists section and I do think it's legit for Gaki to be Necromancers in the same way that, say, Get are Warriors: they tend to have the right Attributes and Skills to do it. That said it is also *soft* confirmed via the Suffer My Sins Actual Play that Gaki aren't inherently able to perceive or interact with incorporeal brings which is... worrying. <br /> <br /> I'm more bothered by Vorare Soul Eating and Black Heart Emotion Draining which I'm pretty sure won't get any further rules. I'm actually putting together a list of things which would be really impactful if true but such we currently have no rules for and only know about through unreliable narrators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T11:57:50-07:00","id":1544215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances?p=1544214#post1544214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm reserving judgement on the Gaki because there *might* be something like the Abjuration/Binding rules from CofD buried in the Magic or Antagonists section and I do think it's legit for Gaki to be Necromancers in the same way that, say, Get are Warriors: they tend to have the right Attributes and Skills to do it. That said it is also *soft* confirmed via the Suffer My Sins Actual Play that Gaki aren't inherently able to perceive or interact with incorporeal brings which is... worrying.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me necromancers need to be able to do more than just deal with ghosts. If I'm going to classify someone as a necromancer I want them to be able to control zombies at the very least. But like you, I'm holding out hope. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm more bothered by Vorare Soul Eating and Black Heart Emotion Draining which I'm pretty sure won't get any further rules. I'm actually putting together a list of things which would be really impactful if true but such we currently have no rules for and only know about through unreliable narrators. </div> </div> </div>Ya, I'm hoping that there will at least be a soulless condition or something in the book, but it seems less and less likely. <br /> <br /> As more and more comes out I feel more and more like this is the Essence version of Chronicles of Darkness, and not entirely in a good way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T12:28:57-07:00","id":1544217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances?p=1544215#post1544215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me necromancers need to be able to do more than just deal with ghosts. If I'm going to classify someone as a necromancer I want them to be able to control zombies at the very least. But like you, I'm holding out hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Old <b>Mage: the Awakening </b>books pointed <i>Moros</i> Path as Necromancers - as those SPEAKING to ghosts. The same was with <i>Council of Bones</i> in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> 2E.<br /> <br /> By word definition - only speaking with, and probably, perceiving ghosts make you necromancer. ( In classical terms. )<br /> <br /> Also, we do not have full rules on Phantasms ( incorporeal beings, like <b>CoD </b>Ephemera ) - so maybe they will clear that most <b>Curseborne</b> don't see ghosts - and only <i>Geki </i>get this.<br /> <br /> Wikipedia on Necromancy:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Necromancy</b> (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English\" target=\"_blank\">/\u02c8n\u025bkr\u0259m\u00e6nsi/</a>) is the practice of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_(paranormal)\" target=\"_blank\">magic</a> involving communication with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death\" target=\"_blank\">dead</a> by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evocation\" target=\"_blank\">summoning</a> their spirits as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost\" target=\"_blank\">apparitions</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vision_(spirituality)\" target=\"_blank\">visions</a> for the purpose of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divination\" target=\"_blank\">divination</a>; imparting the means to foretell future events and discover hidden knowledge.<br /> (...)<br /> The word necromancy is adapted from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Latin\" target=\"_blank\">Late Latin</a> necromantia: a loan word from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koine_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">post-Classical Greek</a> \u03bd\u03b5\u03ba\u03c1\u03bf\u03bc\u03b1\u03bd\u03c4\u03b5\u03af\u03b1 (nekromante\u00eda, or 'divination through a dead body'), a compound of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Greek</a> \u03bd\u03b5\u03ba\u03c1\u03cc\u03c2 (nekr\u00f3s, or 'dead body') and \u03bc\u03b1\u03bd\u03c4\u03b5\u03af\u03b1 (mante\u00eda, or 'divination').\u200b</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-18T12:58:35-07:00","id":1544221,"title":"","content":"Ironically this thread is drifting a bit away from my original intent into something else I was also planning on starting a thread about.<br /> <br /> FWIW here's a summary of what I believe we *know* about Necromancy, Soul-Eating and Emotion-Draining in Curseborne.<ul><li>We know Phantasms are a thing (released chapters)</li> <li>We know some spells affect incorporeal entities (released chapters)</li> <li>We know Zombies exist as antagonists (ashcan)</li> <li>We know drones - people with no soul and little will - exist (ashcan)</li> <li>We know some spells can alter a person's emotional state (released chapters and ashcan)</li> <li>The Gaki inheritance lets them summon a phantasm</li> <li>The Gaki Secret Spell lets them attract the attention of incorporeal entities</li> </ul>Here's what I think we can reasonably assume<ul><li>Vorare soul-eating and Black Heart emotion-draining are unlikely to have bespoke rules (dev responses and actual plays)</li> <li>Gaki don't seem to have an inherent ability to interact with incorporeal beings (Suffer My Sins actual play)</li> <li>A bit of a stretch but I think sound: the Gaki have a Motif which lets them remove the Physical tag from some spells, which I think *probably* implies that this will let them cast spells on incorporeal entities that they otherwise couldn't. [I misremembered, it's clearer than that, they ignore the Incorporeal tag of the targets of Physical spells, which implies the same thing but much more strongly].</li> <li>Some of this is likely to change before launch</li> </ul>Although I also like zombies-necromancy, I don't mind ghosts-only either and I wouldn't be upset if the Gaki were ghosts-only because that's what their flavour text seems to imply. I'd be upset if the Ritual Magic section or the expanded Spells section of the rules didn't build on that (there's some implication that individual spells have upgrade paths in which case Forbidden Temptation might be able to do more than just uselessly attract ghosts you can't perceive or interact with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-18-2024, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T00:36:41-07:00","id":1544264,"title":"","content":"Yep, presently it's a part of the character you adopt or sacrifice depending on the way you want to build them. Will that be the case up through every tier of Entanglement? Will you be able to mix up your Inheritances even more? We will have to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T04:38:41-07:00","id":1544275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances?p=1544217#post1544217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Old <b>Mage: the Awakening </b>books pointed <i>Moros</i> Path as Necromancers - as those SPEAKING to ghosts. The same was with <i>Council of Bones</i> in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> 2E.<br /> <br /> By word definition - only speaking with, and probably, perceiving ghosts make you necromancer. ( In classical terms. )<br /> <br /> Also, we do not have full rules on Phantasms ( incorporeal beings, like <b>CoD </b>Ephemera ) - so maybe they will clear that most <b>Curseborne</b> don't see ghosts - and only <i>Geki </i>get this.<br /> <br /> Wikipedia on Necromancy:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Necromancy</b> (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English\" target=\"_blank\">/\u02c8n\u025bkr\u0259m\u00e6nsi/</a>) is the practice of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_(paranormal)\" target=\"_blank\">magic</a> involving communication with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death\" target=\"_blank\">dead</a> by <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evocation\" target=\"_blank\">summoning</a> their spirits as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost\" target=\"_blank\">apparitions</a> or <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vision_(spirituality)\" target=\"_blank\">visions</a> for the purpose of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Divination\" target=\"_blank\">divination</a>; imparting the means to foretell future events and discover hidden knowledge.<br /> (...)<br /> The word necromancy is adapted from <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Late_Latin\" target=\"_blank\">Late Latin</a> necromantia: a loan word from the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koine_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">post-Classical Greek</a> \u03bd\u03b5\u03ba\u03c1\u03bf\u03bc\u03b1\u03bd\u03c4\u03b5\u03af\u03b1 (nekromante\u00eda, or 'divination through a dead body'), a compound of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Greek\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Greek</a> \u03bd\u03b5\u03ba\u03c1\u03cc\u03c2 (nekr\u00f3s, or 'dead body') and \u03bc\u03b1\u03bd\u03c4\u03b5\u03af\u03b1 (mante\u00eda, or 'divination').</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you're coming off as trying to correct my opinion here, and being kind of shitty about it. <br /> <br /> If I cared what Mage said about Necromancers I'd go post on the Mage forum. I don't. I do however know that the Moros can do a hell of a lot more than just talk to the dead, if you're going to come at me like this at least try and be intellectually honest. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't care what something meant hundreds or even thousands of years ago when I'm using the word in a modern way to discuss a game. Languages change with time, acting otherwise is also intellectually dishonest. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T04:43:58-07:00","id":1544277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances?p=1544264#post1544264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, presently it's a part of the character you adopt or sacrifice depending on the way you want to build them. Will that be the case up through every tier of Entanglement? Will you be able to mix up your Inheritances even more? We will have to see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I get that. And sometimes that feels reasonable and intentional and sometimes it feels janky or just plain unfun.<br /> <br /> Quite often the things you're asked to sacrifice feel like pretty core parts of the fantasy (even in some cases things the flavour text says all members of the Lineage *should* be able to do automatically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T07:01:30-07:00","id":1544288,"title":"","content":"They are indeed core. That's what makes them sacrifices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T07:11:21-07:00","id":1544290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544198-inheritances?p=1544288#post1544288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are indeed core. That's what makes them sacrifices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, but I that case would you mind clarifying what the design intent is behind those sacrifices?<br /> <br /> From a player experience perspective, what am I meant to gain from having to decide whether or not the fact my Dead character is a ghost puppeting a corpse has a game mechanical effect or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}